Yay! This was my first wishless ascension, and first ascension with a
Gnome as well.  "Porrima" is a star in the constellation Virgo.

I suck at writing NH stories so I'll summarize my memories briefly here:

* Lots of amulets were lying around in the dungeon. I found my first
  amulet, of unchanging, on level two or three.  I found at least three
  amulets of unchanging but I didn't feel like polying into a monster.
  An amulet of ESP was very nice in the early game.

* Lots of scrolls of charging.  Not very much scrolls of enchant armor.
  To my surprise an unicorn horn polymorphed into a magic marker when
  dipping into unidentified potions.  I got my second magic marker when
  I polypiled unicorn horns.

* No potions or wands of enlightenment.

* I found the entrance to the Ludios on level 13 but I didn't want to do
  it without reflection.  Eventually a monster dropped a shield of
  reflection.=20

* Ludios had both gray and silver dragons, and both left scales.  I went
  for gray.=20

* I sacrificed fairly much and got first Giantslayer and then Vorpal
  Blade in minetown, where my pet dragon had killed the priest, and then
  I converted the altar to neutral.  Then I found Frost Brand in the
  Valley of the Dead and Fire Brand emerged on the Astral Plane, but I
  didn't use it any more -- I didn't stay to pick it up (see below).

* I got crowned, which I didn't mean to, but it wasn't too bad

* I chose two-weaponing in the end, first with Vorpal and later with
  Frost Brand, using a silver sabre as the secondary weapon.

* I like pets and tried to convert cats and dogs into more powerful
  creatures.  Xorns are nice except for the fact that they eat most
  armour and weapons before you can get them yourself; I like
  disenchanters as general pets.  I fed one disenchanter wraith corpses
  but I lost it somehow.  I found a magic harp which I used to get more
  pets and that's how I acquired Tas the purple worm on Astral.

* Polypiling!  I tried to polypile in the earnest in Ludios and the
  castle.  Results: agreeable.  I got a helm of brilliance that way, the
  only one in the game.  I had found speed boots and gauntlets of power
  somewhere but I ditched the gauntlets when I tried to begin to use
  spells...  I also polypiled for an amulet of reflection (I seem to
  recall).

* I had no offensive spells, really.  I polymorphed spellbooks and got
  identify and remove curse that way.

