* I was glad I could get the fail rate of cure sickess to 0%.

* I made a few mistakes, I think I was distracted or just pressing keys
  too quickly.  Worth mentioning: First, falling into water on the fake
  portal level in Gehennom which blanked few scrolls but, more
  importantly, diluted the alchemized potions of full healing to water.
  Secondly, letting a master mind flayer to suck my brain and forgetting
  levels (re-identifying was easy enough with the spell).  Thirdly,
  losing my +3 speed boots.  I realized, when fighting the high priest
  of Moloch and Rodney in Sanctum that I had still my water walking
  boots on; I switched to them on Juiblex's swamp.  I could not find
  them again but I decided to try it without being very fast.  I had
  diluted my potions of speed ages ago.  Then I found a potion of speed
  on Astral which helped the rush to the altar guarded by Death. -- I
  also had displaced an oilskin sack but I didn't fall into water any
  more.

* Rodney double-troubled many times in Sanctum but not after that.

* The mysterious force threw me around maybe for ten times or slightly
  more.

* Genoless conduct lets one deal with master and arch-liches, which are
  at least a nuisance.  With teleport control and teleport scrolls it's
  easy enough to teleport to the upstairs, except on no-teleport
  levels.  Then it's advantageous to have cursed teleport scrolls...

* Wishless conduct may be difficult or not depending how much useful
  loot you find or can polypile... Polyless and wishless, on the other
  hand -- I'm not very keen on that yet.  It's then ironic that I found
  another wand of wishing. :p

* The planes weren't difficult because I had found enough scrolls of
  gold detection.  I could whack the air elementals quickly enough, even
  with AC -20 and not being very fast.

* I went on Astral from right to left: Famine, Pestilence, Death.  The
  last altar was the right one.

* I had a close call near the middle altar.  It was guarded by
  Pestilence and my guardian Angel had just died.  I couldn't kill=20
  Pestilence with the three remaining charges in a wand of death, and I
  had to cure myself using the spell.  Then there were such monsters
  nearby that took me at the time to 33 HP, and I decided to pray.
  Camaxtli cured my illness but not the HP, and I was sure Porrima would
  die.  Then I was still stun, and Pestilence next to me.  I used my
  unicorn horn once, then a second time, and *Pestilence did not attack*
  but just wandered nearby.  I wonder if he was blind, or maybe scared?

  Then I had a chance to grab a !oFH from my bag of holding and then it
  was easy to go on.  Then I charged a /oDeath once more.  Death died
  without her giving me any damage, thanks to dual-wielding.


On the right (the one on the left!) altar, I let Pestilence come next to
me and then I sacrificed the Amulet, just to annoy him...  He'll
probably be mad with the next adventurer on the Astral! ;P

